From e8b4ea70ff960c1e6b2214fa341eb4937c2c6128 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:54:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(path-cli,webmock): `path d` (baseline, webmock, model),
 just recipes; `webmock run <agent>` replays a cell from the committed
 cassettes

path-cli: the `goldens` feature becomes `develop`, holding `path d` (visible
alias `path develop`; `p` plumbing, `d` develop): `path d baseline` (the old
`path goldens`, kept as a hidden `goldens` alias while in-flight scripts move),
and `path d webmock` / `path d model`, which run toolpath-webmock's `webmock`
and toolpath-model's binaries (path-cli is published and cannot depend on the
unpublished crates). A default build has no `d`. One entry point for checking:
`path d baseline check` runs the tests that are the check (cargo test -p
toolpath-goldens, then the path-cli goldens test), so cargo test is the
implementation and the command its thin wrapper. justfile: `just baseline`,
`just webmock`, `just model`; gates, scripts, docs and the CLI help snapshot
follow.

webmock: `webmock run <agent> record|replay --cell <dir>` copies the cell, starts
one server per upstream, sets the agent's switch and (replay) a fake credential,
runs it hermetically and prints EXACT/LOOSE/MISS per request. Requests are masked
before keying (work dir -> the recording's placeholder), and the loose key drops
<system-reminder> blocks. Copilot's GitHub user answer is committed, identity
replaced. Replay from the committed cassettes: copilot 10/10 exact, claude loose,
both with the recorded reply. pr/53.
